From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drmhwc: retire inherited sprd-dispc planes on first composition

A compositor takeover may inherit an active OSD plane while the new modeset
selects IMG. Both fetches remain enabled unless OSD is explicitly disabled,
so the kernel correctly rejects the first modeset under its RGB fetch budget.
On the single-CRTC sprd-dispc device, include compatible available planes in
the first composition's unused list. Disable them in the same atomic commit;
advance the takeover state only after a successful non-test commit. Respect
pipeline bindings and leave other drivers unchanged.

Assisted-by: GPT-6 (Codex)
---
diff --git a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
index 99d646f..8483b39 100644
--- a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
+++ b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
@@ -439,6 +439,24 @@ bool DrmAtomicStateManager::SetCompositionIfNeeded(const AtomicCommitArgs &args,
   // Initialize the list of unused planes to all the planes used in the
   // previous frame.
   auto unused_planes = committed_frame_state_.used_planes;
+  // sprd-dispc has one CRTC. On takeover the previous composer may have
+  // left OSD enabled, while our first modeset selects IMG. Retire inherited
+  // planes in the same atomic request so the fetch-budget check sees only
+  // the intended composition. Never touch planes bound to another pipeline.
+  if (!committed_frame_state_.composition_set &&
+      pipe_->device->GetName() == "sprd-dispc") {
+    for (const auto &plane : pipe_->device->GetPlanes()) {
+      if (!plane->IsCrtcSupported(*pipe_->crtc->Get())) {
+        continue;
+      }
+      auto binding = plane->BindPipeline(pipe_, true);
+      if (binding && std::find(unused_planes.begin(), unused_planes.end(),
+                               binding) == unused_planes.end()) {
+        unused_planes.emplace_back(std::move(binding));
+      }
+    }
+  }
+  request.new_frame_state.composition_set = true;
   // Clear the list of planes for the next frame. It will be repopulated below.
   request.new_frame_state.used_planes.clear();
 
diff --git a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.h b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.h
index 4e1eb9e..390a02e 100644
--- a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.h
+++ b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.h
@@ -73,6 +73,9 @@ class DrmAtomicStateManager : public DrmAtomicCommitSink {
     /* Required to cleanup unused planes */
     std::vector<std::shared_ptr<BindingOwner<DrmPlane>>> used_planes;
 
+    /* First composition must also retire inherited hardware plane state. */
+    bool composition_set{};
+
     /* To avoid setting the inactive state twice, which will fail the commit */
     bool crtc_active_state{};
   };
